{"format":"hologram.registry.artifact/v1","id":"mcr.microsoft.com/windows/insider","fetched":"2026-09-25T12:12:17.271Z","source":{"name":"Microsoft Artifact Registry","api":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/api/v1/catalog/windows/insider/details?reg=mar","page":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/windows/insider/about"},"readme":"## About\nThis is a base image for Windows Server containers. This image carries the **insider version** of the Windows base OS image.\n\n## Featured Tags\n+ None\n\n## Related Repositories\n+ [windows](https://store.docker.com/images/microsoft-windows): Production version of this base OS image\n+ [windows/nanoserver/insider](https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/windows/nanoserver/insider/about): Insider version of the Nano Server base OS image\n+ [windows/servercore/insider](https://mcr.microsoft.com/en-us/product/windows/servercore/insider/about): Insider version of the Windows Server Core base OS image\n\n## Configuration\n- Your host must have the Windows container feature enabled. The Windows container feature is only available on Windows Server 2016 (Core and with Desktop Experience), Windows 10 Professional and Enterprise (Anniversary Edition) and later.\n- If you intend to run the container with Hyper-V isolation, The Hyper-V role must be installed on the host first.\n\n## Usage\nWindows requires the host OS version to match the container OS version. If you want to run a container based on a newer Windows build, make sure you have an equivalent host build. Otherwise, you can use Hyper-V isolation to run older containers on new host builds. You can read more on Windows Container Version Compatibility in our [Container Docs](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/virtualization/windowscontainers/deploy-containers/version-compatibility).\n\nThe default entrypoint is for this image is Cmd.exe. To run the image:\n\ndocker run `mcr.microsoft.com/windows/insider:10.0.{build}.{revision}`\n\n**Note: This repo does not publish or maintain a** `latest` **tag. Please declare a specific tag when pulling or referencing images from this repo.**\n\n## Support\nFor support or general questions, please post in our [forum](https://social.msdn.microsoft.com/Forums/en-US/home?forum=windowscontainers).\n\n## Feedback\nPlease direct all feedback to our [forum](https://social.msdn.microsoft.com/Forums/en-US/home?forum=windowscontainers).\n\nSuggestions on improving Windows Containers or issues can also be raised at the [repo](https://github.com/microsoft/Windows-Containers).\n\n\n## License\n- Legal Notice: [Container License Information](https://aka.ms/mcr/osslegalnotice)\n\n**MICROSOFT CONTAINER BASE IMAGE**  \n**Preview**. This limited license only gives you some rights to use the software. Microsoft reserves all other rights. You may use this preview, insider, beta or other pre-release versions (“previews”) of the container base image that Microsoft may make available to you. You may use previews only up to the software’s expiration date and so long as you comply with all the terms of this agreement.  \n\nPreviews are experimental and may be substantially different from the commercially released version. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this agreement, **previews are provided “AS IS,” and no warranty, implied or express (including the Limited Warranty), applies to these versions.** Microsoft may not provide support services for previews. If you provide Microsoft comments, suggestions or other feedback about the preview, you grant Microsoft and its partners rights to use the submission in any way and for any purpose. This preview is limited to evaluation purposes (or test or demonstration) use, you may not sell the software, use it in a live operating environment, or use it after the evaluation period. Notwithstanding anything to the contrary in this agreement, **evaluation software is provided “AS IS.”** \n\n**WIP PROGRAM AGREEMENT, Section 10**  \n**Reservation of Rights.** Microsoft may have patents, patent applications, trademarks, copyrights, or other intellectual property rights covering subject matter in the WIP Services. Except as expressly provided in any written license agreement from Microsoft, the furnishing of the WIP Services does not give you any license to these patents, trademarks, copyrights, or other intellectual property. Microsoft reserves all rights not expressly granted under this Agreement, and no other rights are granted under this Agreement by implication or estoppel or otherwise.","readmeBase":null,"publisher":{"name":"Microsoft","url":"https://mcr.microsoft.com/","official":true,"verified":true},"registered":null,"updated":"2021-04-01T22:51:29.7868156+00:00","categories":[],"keywords":[],"license":"Other","links":[{"name":"licence","url":"https://www.microsoft.com/licensing/terms/productoffering/WindowsServerStandardDatacenterEssentials/EAEAS#LicenseModel"}],"maintainers":[],"stats":{"pulls":null,"pullsText":"539K+","stars":null},"mediaTypes":[],"contentTypes":[],"storage":null,"tags":[{"name":"10.0.20324.3","digest":"sha256:6c8e8740d85205c3e4f0480c11edd0e1692f5f68485655182daa06e10140c304","pushed":"2021-04-01T22:51:30.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"10.0.20324.3-amd64","digest":"sha256:9ec32517ef164a15148f07d1302c348edb832c23c7c27090afbf7d1a36e95a57","pushed":"2021-04-01T22:51:07.0000000+00:00","size":626,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"10.0.20317.1","digest":"sha256:7ce2df803bf3c2775b7c0ac51514a895f71a5a278c67425dc1e9a1cd88fad02d","pushed":"2021-03-25T18:11:11.0000000+00:00","size":null,"platforms":[],"mediaType":"application/vnd.docker.distribution.manifest.list.v2+json","status":null},{"name":"10.0.20317.1-amd64","digest":"sha256:3173e0ff65b66c099c69c99ff32bb46d474113b07ca5fd6d5e582f4109fd06b7","pushed":"2021-03-25T18:10:48.0000000+00:00","size":626,"platforms"